      "citations": null,
      "text": "The RMW factor is the average of the two robust (high-OP) portfolio returns minus the average of the two weak (low-OP) portfolio returns, using the value-weighted monthly returns. The script parses only the value-weighted monthly block and skips the equal-weighted block and the annual sections.\n\n```python\nimport csv\nimport math\n\nIN_FILE = \"6_Portfolios_ME_OP_2x3.csv\"\nOUT_FILE = \"output.csv\"\n\n\ndef is_missing(x):\n    return x is None or math.isnan(x) or abs(x + 99.99) < 1e-6 or abs(x + 999.0) < 1e-6\n\n\ndef parse_value_weighted_block(path):\n    with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\") as f:\n        lines = f.read().splitlines()\n\n    # locate the monthly value-weighted block\n    start = None\n    for i, line in enumerate(lines):\n        low = line.lower()\n        if \"value weighted\" in low and \"monthly\" in low:\n            start = i\n            break\n    if start is None:\n        raise RuntimeError(\"Could not find monthly value-weighted block\")\n\n    rows = []\n    started = False\n    for line in lines[start + 1:]:\n        parts = [p.strip() for p in line.split(\",\")]\n        if parts and len(parts[0]) == 6 and parts[0].isdigit() and len(parts) >= 7:\n            started = True\n            date = int(parts[0])\n            vals = []\n            for p in parts[1:7]:\n                try:\n                    v = float(p)\n                except ValueError:\n                    v = float(\"nan\")\n                if is_missing(v):\n                    v = float(\"nan\")\n                vals.append(v)\n            rows.append((date, vals))\n        else:\n            if started:\n                # end of monthly value-weighted block\n                break\n    return rows\n\n\ndef main():\n    rows = parse_value_weighted_block(IN_FILE)\n\n    # column order in file: SMALL LoOP, ME1 OP2, SMALL HiOP, BIG LoOP, ME2 OP2, BIG HiOP\n    SMALL_LO, SMALL_HI, BIG_LO, BIG_HI = 0, 2, 3, 5\n\n    out = []\n    for date, vals in rows:\n        sl, sh = vals[SMALL_LO], vals[SMALL_HI]\n        bl, bh = vals[BIG_LO], vals[BIG_HI]\n        if any(math.isnan(x) for x in (sl, sh, bl, bh)):\n            continue\n        rmw = 0.5 * (sh + bh) - 0.5 * (sl + bl)\n        out.append((date, rmw))\n\n    out.sort(key=lambda r: r[0])\n\n    with open(OUT_FILE, \"w\", newline=\"\") as f:\n        w = csv.writer(f)\n        w.writerow([\"date\", \"value\"])\n        for date, val in out:\n            w.writerow([date, repr(float(val))])\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
